<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahendra of Nepal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–1972</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as King Mahendra, Mahendra Bir Bikram Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahendra was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> from 1955 until his death in 1972. In December 1960 he dismissed the elected government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/b-p-koirala">B. P. Koirala</a>, banned political parties and in 1962 introduced the partyless panchayat system, which concentrated power in the monarchy for the next three decades. He also promoted Nepali national identity, launched the East–West Highway and balanced Nepal's relations between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahendra-of-nepal.jpg" alt="Mahendra of Nepal" width="320" height="549" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archive Nepal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Mahendra_of_Nepal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
